    "body": "🤖 **Agent note** · triaged (task 12432, lane code-x, direct)\n\n**Verdict: REAL AND CURRENT — the public-domain normalization has not been recorded anywhere, and no work item carried it. Converted to a follow-up packet (below).**\n\nFresh evidence this shift (2026-11-08):\n- Issue #6009 OPEN, no hard-stop labels, no matching PR. Parent topic issue #5977 OPEN (its triage, task 12417, was handed to the opencode claimant earlier this shift).\n- Nothing landed: `git grep` at current main finds no `CC0-1.0`, `0BSD`, or public-domain normalization in `pkgs/id/src`, `pkgs/id/contract`, or the `doc/` design records, and there is no license-taxonomy module in `pkgs/id/src` yet. (Hits in a vendored crates dataset are third-party license metadata, not repo code.)\n- The prior triage (task 10375, 2026-11-05) confirmed the design as well-scoped and directed that the resolved mapping be carried into the #5977 taxonomy spec before that parent design is finalized — but created no work item, so the decision has sat unowned since. That is the gap Drew's triage doctrine (code#7016) exists to close.\n\n**Routing:** follow-up task 12998 (small_fix, dedupe `repo-health:v1:fix:developing-today/code:issue:6009`): land the normalization rule (content → CC0-1.0, code → 0BSD/Unlicense, never a bare \"public domain\" string) + the one-sentence plain-language UI copy into the #5977 taxonomy spec/design record — or, if that record does not exist when claimed, as linked design notes on issues #5977 and #6009 so the parent cannot finalize without it. Issue #6009 stays OPEN; it closes via that adoption, never via triage.\n<!-- agent-note:v1 agent=repo-worker-code-x state=triaged at=2026-11-08T06:03:00Z -->\n",
